# Line-ending and diff policy.
#
# Why this file exists: the repo had none, while core.autocrlf was true. That made line
# endings a property of each developer's machine rather than of the repo, which (a) makes
# merges and cherry-picks noisier than they need to be -- material when ~541 upstream commits
# are still to be ported -- and (b) would diverge between a Windows dev box and a Linux CI
# runner. Verified before adding this: no binary asset was ever mis-stored as text.

# Normalize every text file to LF in the index AND in the working tree, so behaviour is
# identical on Windows, Linux CI, and macOS regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts whose interpreter cares about line endings.
*.bat        text eol=crlf
*.cmd        text eol=crlf
*.sh         text eol=lf
gradlew      text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalize, never diff as text.
# (3498 .png / 66 .mp3 / 31 .ogg / 10 .jpg / 3 .ttf at time of writing.)
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.ogg        binary
*.mp3        binary
*.wav        binary
*.ttf        binary
*.otf        binary
*.jar        binary
*.apk        binary
*.aab        binary
*.keystore   binary
*.jks        binary
*.dat        binary
*.zip        binary
*.so         binary

# Better diff hunk headers: git shows the enclosing class/function on each hunk.
*.java       diff=java
*.kt         diff=java
*.kts        diff=java
*.html       diff=html
*.md         diff=markdown

# Save fixtures are binary by intent -- a textual diff of one is meaningless and a
# normalized one is a corrupted test fixture.
SPD-classes/src/test/resources/save-fixtures/** binary
